# Leads

- Signup success = Supabase insert succeeded. Log Resend/notification failures; do not show them to the visitor.
- Service-role key and Resend key are server-only. Browser env uses the publishable/anon key, never the service role.
- RLS stays ON on lead tables. No public read policies. Inserts go through App Router route handlers.
- Missing Supabase in local/dev: return the existing user-safe error. Do not throw stack traces or invent a second storage path.
- Keep honeypot, rate limit, and payload-size guards in `formGuard.ts` on public POST routes.
